#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# quadratic_optimization

#% text
# `quadratic_optimization(f, cons, vars)` gives the point `[x -> ..., y -> ...]` that minimizes the convex quadratic `f` under the constraints `cons`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `cons` is one condition or a list of them (equalities, inequalities and chains such as `1 <= y <= 2`); `vars` is the list of the variables.

#% item
# A fourth argument selects the result: "PrimalMinimumValue", "PrimalMinimizer" (the values only), "PrimalMinimizerRules" (the default), or a list of these.

#% item
# `quadratic_optimization([q, c], [a, b])` minimizes `x . q . x/2 + c . x` under `a . x + b >= 0`, and `quadratic_optimization([q, c], [a, b], [aeq, beq])` also under `aeq . x + beq == 0`; the result is the vector `x`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
quadratic_optimization(x^2 + y^2, [x + y == 2, 1 <= y, y <= 2], [x, y])
#% output
#= [x -> 1, y -> 1]

#% cell
quadratic_optimization(x^2 + y^2, x + y >= 1, [x, y], "PrimalMinimumValue")
#% output
#= 1/2

#% cell
quadratic_optimization(2*x^2 + 20*y^2 + 6*x*y + 5*x, [-x + y >= 2, y >= 0], [x, y], ["PrimalMinimumValue", "PrimalMinimizer"])
#% output
#= [-449/112, [-97/56, 15/56]]

#% cell
quadratic_optimization([[[2, 0], [0, 2]], [0, 0]], [[[1, 1]], [-1]])
#% output
#= [1/2, 1/2]

